SUMMARY:Intermediate Ride (C) - Conestoga Cruisin' CROPPED (37F)
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\n**Be Safe\, Have Fun\, an
 d Ride Together**\n\n**Ride leader: Volunteer to lead!**\n**Ride sweep: TB
 D**\n\n**Anticipated Average Pace: (14-16 mph)**\n\n[https://ridewithgps.c
 om/routes/](https://ridewithgps.com/routes/57663538)\n**THIS IS A CROPPED 
 VERSION of Conestoga Cruisin' 50. The 50 mile version is CP's IMPROMPTU bi
 rthday ride today! You can choose this shorter version and still celebrate
  with CP and friends! The routes are together until mile 25.5 (just past S
 heetz in New Holland). It picks the route up again at 28 miles.**\n\n**Thi
 s is an Intermediate C Class ride. Ride leaders will ride within the adver
 tised average speed range. This is intended to be a group ride with a no-d
 rop rule as the main goal. Riders are encouraged to ride in a group or gro
 ups\, based on paces. If there is no sweep\, do not drop individual riders
  off the back. Ride leaders will do their best to keep the group together 
 with occasional regroupings and/or splitting into multiple groups to align
  to paces.**\n\n**Helmets are mandatory. No earbuds. Please bring water an
 d a basic repair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump/CO2 inflator).**\n\n
 **To eliminate passing around a pen and paper waiver\, we require LBC Club
  membership and Meetup RSVP below to join this ride. Being on Meetup does 
 not mean you are a club member. Join here** [Member Signup](https://www.la
 ncasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)\n\n**Your RSVP
  is your agreement to abide by the club's Code of Conduct:** [Code of Cond
 uct](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257
 148&module_id=323984)\n\n**Guidance if an incident occurs:** [Incident Act
 ions](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148
 &module_id=326137)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-bicycle-club/events/3171036
 83/
